<title>USA: ICU Medical Q3 shr rises to $0.11.</title>
<headline>ICU Medical Q3 shr rises to $0.11.</headline>
<dateline>SAN CLEMENTE, Calif 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statements of Income</p>
<p>	 For the Three and Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>	  Sept. 30, 1996, and Sept. 30, 1995</p>
<p>(all dollar amounts in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>			(unaudited)</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended     Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>			   9/30/96     9/30/95    9/30/96   9/30/95</p>
<p> Net sales	     $  5,972   $  4,617   $ 18,127  $ 16,010</p>
<p> Cost of sales	    2,884	2,307	8,043     8,170</p>
<p> Gross profit	     3,088	2,310     10,084     7,840</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>administrative expenses</p>
<p>				1,888	1,149	5,021     4,198</p>
<p>Income from operations</p>
<p>				1,200	1,161	5,063     3,642</p>
<p>Interest and other income</p>
<p>				  330	  260	1,003	 411</p>
<p> Income before tax	1,530	1,421	6,066     4,053</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes</p>
<p>				  566	  530	2,244     1,540</p>
<p> Net income		   964	  891	3,822     2,513</p>
<p>Earnings per common and</p>
<p>common stock equivalent:</p>
<p> Net income per share    0.11	 0.10	 0.43	0.32</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>and common equivalent</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>			  8,907,056  8,890,485  8,992,433 7,968,161</p>
<p>NOTE: Net sales do not include revenue sharing under the company's agreement with Abbott Laboratories Inc. The company expects to start reporting those revenues in its fourth quarter.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
